    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "The diagnostic criteria used by Lorish et al., in their analysis of 13 patients included the following: 1. A prodrome of stiffness and rigidity in axial muscles. 2. Slow progression of stiffness to include proximal limb muscles making volitional movements and ambulation difficult. 3. A fixed deformity of the spine. 4. The presence of superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movement, jarring, noise, and emotional upsets. 5. Normal findings on motor and sensory nerve examination. Normal intellect. 7. Typical electromyographic finding of continuous motor activity abolished by the intravenous administration of diazepam, or a positive response to a therapeutic of trial of orally administered diazepam.",
      "quote": "The diagnostic criteria used by Lorish et al.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
